{"full":"hf:Caoyunkang/AdaCLIP","spaceId":"Caoyunkang/AdaCLIP","name":"AdaCLIP -- Zero-shot Anomaly Detection","source":"huggingface","description":"Detecting visual anomalies for novel categories! ","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":15,"created":"2024-07-20T15:55:52.000Z","updated":"2024-07-24T09:07:57.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://caoyunkang-adaclip.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Caoyunkang/AdaCLIP","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:41.890Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:41.890Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:41.890Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[ECCV 24] AdaCLIP: Adapting CLIP with Hybrid Learnable Prompts for Zero-Shot Anomaly Detection. by Yunkang Cao, Jiangning Zhang, Luca Frittoli, Yuqi Cheng, Weiming Shen, Giacomo Boracchi","Zero-shot anomaly detection (ZSAD) targets the identification of anomalies within images from arbitrary novel categories. This study introduces AdaCLIP for the ZSAD task, leveraging a pre-trained vision-language model (VLM), CLIP. AdaCLIP incorporates learnable prompts into CLIP and optimizes them through training on auxiliary annotated anomaly detection data. Two types of learnable prompts are proposed: \\textit{static} and \\textit{dynamic}. Static prompts are shared across all images, serving to preliminarily adapt CLIP for ZSAD. In contrast, dynamic prompts are generated for each test…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Caoyunkang/AdaCLIP/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7f91e021816dc5190b56e89e23fb7c17e368500255ed82bca0f2fda6bfb65c52","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T21:04:36.336Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T02:44:41.916Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"[ECCV 24] AdaCLIP: Adapting CLIP with Hybrid Learnable Prompts for Zero-Shot Anomaly Detectio